Introduction
& codeine; Screenshot
Screenshot
& codeine; is a simple media player using Phonon technology. & codeine; is a no frills media player that excels at playing DVDs and movie files without getting in your way.
Menu and Command Reference
The Play Menu
Ctrl; O Play...
Opens the Play Media dialog, allowing you to Play a DVD, VCD or a video file.
Space Play
If a movie is loaded, this option allows you to pause and resume playback.
S Play Stop
If a movie is loaded, this option allows you to stop playback.
Ctrl; Q Play Quit
Quits & codeine;.
The Settings Menu
F Settings
While playing a movie, you can enter full screen mode. This uses the entire monitor to display the movie
Settings Aspect Ratio
This menu lets you pick the aspect ratio of the playing movie. The aspect ratio is width of movie compared to the height.
Settings Subtitles
This menu is active if there are any subtitles available from the currently playing movie. Note that it may take a few seconds of playback before the subtitles become available.
Settings Audio Channels
This menu is active if there are any additional audio channels available. For instance, some DVDs have additional languages. Note that it may take a few seconds of playback before the audio channels become available.
R Settings
To be written
Settings Videosettings
Settings Configure Shortcuts...
Allows you to configure the & codeine; shortcuts.
Settings Configure Toolbars...
Allows you to configure what buttons are available on the toolbar.
Settings Show Toolbar
Enables or disable the main application toolbar.
